  "definition": "Delisting Procedure for Wines in State Liquor Stores",
  "effectiveDate": "2024-07-03",
  "historyNote": "(See Revision Note #1 and Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Liq 300) #14018, eff 7-3-24",
  "inScheme": "https://granitestate.github.io/rules/scheme",
  "notation": "Liq 304.06",
  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/liq100-1100.html",
  "prefLabel": "Liq 304.06 Delisting Procedure for Wines in State Liquor Stores",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Liq 304.06 Delisting Procedure for Wines in State Liquor Stores.\n\n(a) For purposes of a recurring review, the division shall determine the required minimum gross profit threshold during the preceding, rolling 12-month period and shall regularly inform all liquor and wine representatives and manufacturers of the minimum threshold necessary to reach primary, secondary, and tertiary listing status.\n\n(b) Any wine included as a primary, secondary, or tertiary listing in the state liquor stores shall be subject to a recurring review to ensure that it is listed at the appropriate level.\n\n(c) Failure of any listed wine to meet at least the required minimum gross profit required during any recurring review shall result in delisting of the product and depletion as provided in Liq 302.08.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1 and Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Liq 300) #14018, eff 7-3-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/liq100-1100.html"
